  "storage": "Keep in an airtight jar in a cool, dark cupboard; buy small pouches because ground spices fade within a few months.",
  "looksLike": "A fine dark-brown to almost black powder with an oily, slightly clumpy texture. It smells sweet-smoky rather than hot, because it is made from roasted coriander, sesame, dry coconut and whole spices including dagad phool (stone flower).",
  "howToPick": "The powder should be dark, fragrant and fine with a roasted, sweet-spiced smell. Avoid a faded, flat smell or damp clumps. Brands differ a lot in dagad phool and coconut content, so buying a pouch from a Maharashtrian brand is closest to the traditional flavour.",
  "shelfLife": "About 6 to 12 months sealed, and stronger in the first few months (general guidance; not taken from a source in this run).",
